reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, $3$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $3.$" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373121 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373122 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373123 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373124 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373125 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1041 "selection" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373121 13194139535895 true] [17592186373120 1110 #uuid "5d352153-f300-51f5-a9c8-1078d7781ec0" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373121 1034 "3" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373121 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535895 true] [17592186373121 1111 #uuid "6a8284fd-e415-559a-9499-67de3827fa8c" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373122 1034 "2" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373122 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535895 true] [17592186373122 1111 #uuid "e19eef0e-99a8-52a2-b435-adbbcb326e75" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373123 1034 "6" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373123 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535895 true] [17592186373123 1111 #uuid "fb2edaa6-2836-5984-b3dc-4910fcaaab15" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373124 1034 "1" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373124 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535895 true] [17592186373124 1111 #uuid "4258eb00-b147-5416-b5e1-70fc0e5154ad" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373125 1034 "0" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373125 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535895 true] [17592186373125 1111 #uuid "adb27dcf-1508-5c7b-bc52-6d0a29b267f6" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373127 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1089 "q-79326" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1100 "Let ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}+{v}_{4}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$\n- $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}})=4$\n- $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4},w})=5$" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1113 #uuid "20b472e3-9e5e-5f24-9f58-3446c6fe971d" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373126 1145 "Recall that a basis of a vector space $V$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that span $V.$ The dimension of $V$ is the number of vectors in any basis of $V$ (if such a basis exists). \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is spanned by the vectors by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}.$ Moreover, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ is a basis of the span.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$, and these are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ is a basis of the span. Therefore, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}})=4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. We are told that $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}+{v}_{4}.$ Hence,$w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}.$ this means that $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4},w}$ is completely spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4}$ only. So, $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},{v}_{4},w})=4$ (not $5$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139535895 true] [17592186373127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373128 13194139535895 true] [17592186373127 1000 #edb/ref 